Chapter: BvtSummonFollowers
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtLeash
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 Two daemons summoned by one caster (5 followers each); the first is deleted as Dispel and [remove delete it. Answers
 the caster's followers with the first gone plus 100 times the followers with both alive; -1 when not built.
  bsfl-followers : Integer -> Integer
  bsfl-followers (unused) = when blh-owner 0
    is Err (_) -> -1
    is Ok (owner) -> let game = owner.checkpoint.game
      in when world-create game.world (gs-mobile 0 1420 1700 0 400 0)
        is Err (_) -> -2
        is Ok (caster) -> let gone = cg-summon owner caster "daemon" 1422 1700 0 True 400000
          in let kept = cg-summon owner caster "daemon" 1418 1700 0 True 400000
          in if gone <= 0 | kept <= 0 then -3
          else let both = cg-followers owner caster
          in when world-delete game.world gone
            is Err (_) -> -4
            is Ok (_) -> cg-followers owner caster + 100 * both
  bvt-summon-followers : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-summon-followers (unused) = act
    n <- bsfl-followers 0
    a <- bvt-check ("a summon deleted by Dispel or [remove frees its followers at once, before the spawn pass reaps its slot (UOAIX-214, soak 2026-10-09; got " & show n & ")") (n >= 0 & int-mod n 100 == 5)
    b <- bvt-check ("two live daemons count 10 followers (got " & show n & ")") (n / 100 == 10)
    a + b
  end